你绝不能简单回答‘我们在作业里证明过有限整环是域’——这当然不行；但如果在判断题部分，绝对可以！关键在于理解是什么决定了命题的真伪，你可以直接引用西罗定理或作业推导过的结论等等作为依据。
' you can't say, 'In the homework we proved that a finite integral domain is a field'—that would be... But in the True/False part, absolutely, the key thing is to understand what makes this statement true or false, and you can quote the material like the Sylow theorems or things that we did in homework and things like that, okay?

34
00:09:34,897 --> 00:09:51,440
是的，只有非常核心基础的定理，我们才可能要求写证明；我们绝不会去考那些需要花整整一节课才能证完的定理。我不想让大家去死记硬背——我不想让你们死记西罗定理的证明。
Yeah, again, it would have to be a fairly central theorem for us to ask the proof, and we're not going to ask the proof of a theorem that takes an entire lecture to do, okay? I don't want you to memorize—I don't want you to memorize the proof of the Sylow theorems.

35
00:09:51,440 --> 00:10:07,013
大家只需了解西罗定理是如何通过群在集合上的作用推导出来的，了解我们如何分类pq 阶群以及 p^2 阶群，而无需背下整套繁琐证明。
It's nice to know how the Sylow theorems come about by a group acting on sets; it's nice to know how we classify groups of order pq and of order p^2, you know, without going through the entire rigmarole, okay?

36
00:10:07,013 --> 00:10:11,344
是的，西罗定理的证明相当复杂，死记硬背毫无意义。
But yeah, the Sylow theorems are quite involved, and it would be ridiculous to memorize.

37
00:10:11,344 --> 00:10:20,740
我本科时上过一门数学课（Math 212），期末考试千篇一律：‘陈述并证明闭图像定理（Closed Graph Theorem），陈述并证明这个定理，
I once had a math class where it just consisted of—it was Math 212 when I was an undergraduate, and the exam was always the same: 'State and prove the Closed Graph Theorem, state and prove this theorem, state and prove that theorem.

38
00:10:20,740 --> 00:10:33,132
陈述并证明那个定理。’于是备考就变成了连续数小时枯坐死背这些极其复杂的证明；结果大家都懂，考完两天后，谢天谢地，你把闭图像定理忘得一干二净。
' So it just consisted of sitting there for hours and hours memorizing these proofs which were incredibly involved, and then, you know, two days later, fortunately, you remember nothing about the Closed Graph Theorem and things like that.

39
00:10:33,132 --> 00:10:54,691
所以我在这里的目标是让大家熟练掌握代数语言；以后翻阅课本时，你能回想起来西罗定理是通过让p-群作用在集合上、分析稳定子群等等方法证明出来的。好了，我们来过一遍核心专题。我今天先复习群论与向量空间。
So I mean, my objective here is so that you become conversant with the language, and so that if you have to go to the book, you could remind yourself that the Sylow theorem was proved by having p-groups act on sets and figuring out what the stabilizer was, and things of that nature, okay? So let's go through the basic topics. So I'm gonna do groups and vector spaces.

40
00:10:54,691 --> 00:11:08,200
正如刚才所说，本学期共有三大板块：群、向量空间与域、以及交换环。
So as I say, there really are three units that we did: groups, vector spaces and fields, and commutative rings.

41
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:27,648
彼得将在周五做环论复习，我今天梳理前两部分。大家随时提问，我将顺着近世代数复习提纲（study sheet）讲下去。首先是群的定义：如果连群的定义都不知道，那我们寸步难行。
Peter will do this review on Friday; I'll try to do the first part now. People should just ask me questions. I'm gonna go down the Abstract Algebra study sheet. So the definition of a group: if we don't have the definition of a group, we're not going to be able to do much.

42
00:11:27,648 --> 00:11:35,064
你应当清楚群是一个带有乘法、单位元、逆元且满足结合律的集合。
So you should know that it's a set with a multiplication, an identity, inverses, and the associative law.

43
00:11:35,064 --> 00:11:48,358
你应当熟知一些群的典型例子，我们在课程中反复使用的是实数域上的 GL_n(R)——即线性代数中可逆矩阵构成的乘法群——以及集合的对称群，
And you should have some examples of groups, and the examples of groups that we used all the time were GL_n over, say, over the reals—the multiplicative group of matrices that we got out of linear algebra—

44
00:11:48,358 --> 00:12:04,913
即集合到自身的全体一一双射。大家应当理解为什么它们构成群。随后，这是群的定义；接着是子群的定义：在乘法下封闭、包含单位元且包含每个元素逆元的子集。
and the symmetry groups of a set, so all bijections (one-to-one maps) of the set to itself. And you should understand why those are groups. And then, so that was the definition of a group.

45
00:12:13,802 --> 00:12:26,070
接着我们引入了群之间的同态与同构概念，并指出同态的核（kernel）是 G 的子群，同态的像（image）是 G' 的子群；
And we had the notion of homomorphisms between groups and isomorphisms between groups, and we identified that the kernel of a homomorphism was a subgroup of G,

46
00:12:26,070 --> 00:12:39,300
其中核是 G 的特殊子群——它是 G 的正规子群（normal subgroup），这正是正规子群的引入背景。
and the image of a homomorphism was a subgroup of G', and that the kernel was a special subgroup of G: it was a normal subgroup of G.

47
00:12:39,300 --> 00:13:06,009
在给出正规子群定义后，我们证明了任一正规子群都能实现为某个同态的核——这是一个重要事实：G 的任一正规子群 H 都是某群同态 f 的核，该同态将 G 映到陪集空间上。
And that was the definition of a normal subgroup. And then after this definition of normal subgroup, we showed that any normal subgroup could be defined as the kernel of a homomorphism—that's an important fact: any normal H in G is the kernel of a homomorphism f, and the homomorphism maps G to the coset space.

48
00:13:06,009 --> 00:13:29,260
大家应当回顾——这是一个重要的抽象概念——对任意子群 H，如何首先将其定义为集合：在 G 上定义等价关系，其等价类即为不同的陪集（cosets）；陪集空间就是等价类的集合。
And so you should recall—and this is an important abstract concept—first of all, how one defines this as a set, for any H, by making an equivalence relation on G whose equivalence classes are the different cosets, and this is the set of equivalence classes, or cosets.

49
00:13:29,260 --> 00:13:45,306
接着，当 H 在 G 中正规时，在乘法 (gH)(g'H) = (gg')H 下它构成一个群。
And then it's a group under the multiplication (gH)(g'H) = (gg')H when H is normal in G.

50
00:13:45,306 --> 00:14:06,058
此时该同态将元素 g 映到 g 关于 H 的陪集 gH；由于正规子群上的这种乘法良定义，它构成了群同态，其核恰为 H，其像为整个商群 G/H（满射）。
And then this homomorphism takes an element g to the coset of g with respect to H, and because of this multiplication law in a normal subgroup, that is a group homomorphism whose kernel is precisely H and whose image is all of G/H, so this is surjective (onto).

51
00:14:06,058 --> 00:14:24,214
随后我们得出了一个重要的计数定理（拉格朗日定理）：若 G 有限，则 |G| = |H| · [G:H]，即子群阶数乘以陪集个数（指数）。
And then we had an important counting theorem that if G is finite, the order |G| is the order of the subgroup |H| times the index [G:H], the number of cosets.

52
00:14:24,214 --> 00:14:37,905
这可以看作通过每个陪集恰好包含 |H| 个元素来对 G 的全体元素计数。这是一个极其有用的计数命题。
And that can be viewed as counting the number of elements here by recognizing that each one of the cosets contains exactly |H| elements. So that was a useful counting proposition.

53
00:14:37,905 --> 00:14:45,990
商群最著名的例子之一——我们曾做过专项研究——是当群 G 为整数加法群 Z 时。
So one of the most famous examples of quotient groups—so we made a special study of it—was when the group G was Z.

54
00:14:45,990 --> 00:15:05,014
我们证明了 Z 的子群 H 只能具有nZ 的形式（n 为整数），其商群即为Z/nZ。
We showed the only subgroups H were of the form nZ for an integer n, and that the quotient group was Z/nZ.

55
00:15:05,014 --> 00:15:22,698
它不仅具有群结构，实际上还具有环结构；但在群论部分中这并不影响：它是一个循环群，由 1 mod n 的等价类生成。
Now this has more structure than just a group: this actually has the structure of a ring, but in the group theory section it didn't make any difference: this was cyclic, generated by the class 1 mod n.

56
00:15:22,698 --> 00:15:35,524
我们深入研究了这个群以及该群上的算术性质，因为它是基准群——正如矩阵群是基准非交换群一样，Z/nZ 是最基础的交换群。
And we made a lot of study of this group and the arithmetic of this group, because it's just a basic group—just as these are basic non-abelian groups, these are very basic abelian groups.

57
00:15:35,524 --> 00:15:57,960
Z是无限阶循环群，而 Z/nZ 是任意有限阶循环群；我们证明了任一 n 阶循环群都同构于这个群，即同构于 Z/nZ。
This is a cyclic group of infinite order, and these are cyclic groups of any finite order. And we showed that an arbitrary cyclic group of order n was isomorphic to this group, is isomorphic to Z/nZ.

58
00:15:57,960 --> 00:16:26,996
如果我要建立同构，只需选取一个生成元——循环群意味着它由某给定元素的全部幂次构成——选取生成元 g，在同态下将 1 mod n 映为 g，将 a mod n 映为元素 g^a。
And if I wanted to make the isomorphism, I would choose a generator—a cyclic group means one that consists of all powers of a given element—so choose a generator g, and you map 1 mod n in the homomorphism to g, and you map a mod n to the element g^a.

59
00:16:26,996 --> 00:16:38,664
这是满射，因为 G 中的每个元素都形如 g的 a 次幂（g^a），且它只依赖于 a 模 n 的余数，因为 g^n 是单位元。
And that's a surjective map because everything in G is of the form g to the a, and it only depends on what a is mod n because g^n is the identity element.

60
00:16:38,664 --> 00:16:48,743
所以……这是基础结论：在同构意义下，对每个正整数 n 只有唯一的 n 阶循环群。
So these are the... This is basic: there's only one cyclic group of order n for every n up to isomorphism.

61
00:16:48,743 --> 00:17:09,771
接着我们暂时告别了群论——转去讲向量空间与域；但从复习的角度，我打算先停留在群论的世界里，基（bases）等内容我们稍后再讲。
And in particular this... So then we took a little tour away from groups—we went to vector spaces and fields, but from the point of view of review, I'm just going to stay inside the world of groups for the moment, and we'll come back to bases and things of that nature later.

62
00:17:09,771 --> 00:17:30,974
在群论中，我们接下来研究了群在集合上的作用这一核心主题：我们着重讲解了群 G 在集合 S 上的作用：在抽象层面上，这不过是群 G 到集合 S 的对称群Sym(S) 的一个群同态；
So we then went on to study other interesting groups as groups acting on sets. So we made a big deal about a group G acting on a set S: this is just a homomorphism from G into the symmetric group Sym(S) abstractly;

63
00:17:30,974 --> 00:17:46,257
换言之，对 G 中任一元素 g 及 S 中任一元素 s，都有一个元素 g(s)落在 S 中，且满足 (gg')(s) = g(g'(s))。
or another way of saying it is, for every g in G and every element s in S, we have an element g(s) in S, and (gg')(s) = g(g'(s)).

64
00:17:46,257 --> 00:17:54,428
这说明它是一个同态，因为对称群中的乘法就是映射的复合。
And that says that this is a homomorphism, because multiplication in the symmetric group of S is just composition of maps.

65
00:17:54,428 --> 00:18:07,840
当群作用在集合上时，我们定义了若干核心概念：我们定义了元素的稳定化子（stabilizer），定义了 s 的轨道（orbit）——它是 S 的子集。
And when we had a group acting on a set, we had various concepts that we defined: we defined the stabilizer of an element, and we defined the orbit of s, which was a subset of S.

66
00:18:07,840 --> 00:18:28,340
稳定化子是 G 的子群，而轨道则同构于陪集空间 G/G_s（轨道-稳定子定理）：将陪集 g G_s 对应到轨道中的元素g(s)（即同轨道的某个 s'）。
The stabilizer was a subgroup of G, and the orbit we identified with the coset space G/G_s by mapping a coset g G_s to the element in the orbit which was g(s), some element s' in the same orbit.

67
00:18:28,340 --> 00:18:33,848
这只依赖于陪集，因为该子群保持 s 不动。
And that only depends on the coset because this subgroup fixes s.

68
00:18:33,848 --> 00:18:47,554
如果群 G 是有限群——更确切地，如果群作用在有限集 S 上，我们可以将 S 分解为 G 的各条轨道的不相交并集。
And if we had a finite group G— well, if we had a group acting on a finite set S, then we could decompose S as the disjoint union of the orbits for G.

69
00:18:47,554 --> 00:19:12,759
因此 S 的元素个数等于各条轨道大小之和，而每条轨道都是一个陪集空间，即各条轨道上稳定子群指数 [G : G_s] 之和。这在许多不同情形下为我们提供了极其强大的计数公式，取决于所考虑的具体作用。
And therefore the cardinality |S| was the sum of the sizes of the different orbits, and each orbit was a coset space; so this was the sum of the indices of the stabilizers [G : G_s] over the different orbits. And this gave us a very useful counting formula in a lot of different situations, depending on what action we took.

70
00:19:12,759 --> 00:19:32,290
关于群作用在集合上的例子：从复习的角度，在脑海中梳理群论时，我真正会把群论划分为三个完全不同的部分：第一是抽象群论——群的定义、同态以及陪集，这完全是纯抽象的符号代数推演；
So, some examples of groups acting on sets: I would really divide group theory, when I was thinking about it for review to organize it in my head, into three completely different sections: there's the abstract group theory—the definitions of the objects,

71
00:19:32,290 --> 00:19:49,896
第二是关于群如何通过作用在集合上产生，即表现为对称群的子群。这是群的一个至关重要的具体实现：群作用在集合上；第三是大量具体的群范例，比如集合的对称群、矩阵构成的线性群、无限阶循环群、有限阶循环群等。
and the homomorphisms and cosets, that's completely abstract, that could be done with a set of symbols, okay? Then there's the theory of the way groups arise acting on sets, and subgroups of the symmetric group of a set. So this is a very important realization of groups: groups acting on sets.

72
00:19:49,896 --> 00:20:10,423
大家必须熟练掌握这些例子；它们有的来自数论（如整数加法群），有的来自群的作用。
And you have to know these examples: some of them come up from number theory, like the integers; some of them come up from group actions.

73
00:20:10,423 --> 00:20:54,269
我们常用的另一个例子是正交群O_n(R)，它是 GL_n(R) 的子群，由保持 R^n 上内积不变的变换组成；若用矩阵表示，就是满足 A A^T = I 的矩阵。我们证明过这意味着正交矩阵的行列式为 ±1。
So another example we used was the orthogonal group O_n(R), which was a subgroup of GL_n(R), and that was the things that preserved an inner product on R^n; or if you put them in terms of matrices, they were the matrices such that A A^T = I. And we saw that implied that the determinant of an orthogonal matrix was ±1.

74
00:20:54,269 --> 00:21:14,890
我们学过这个群；接着我们讲了刚体运动群（group of motions），它是正交群的扩充——正交群作用在 R^n 上，保持线性结构与内积，特别地保持向量空间的原点不动；
So we had that group. And then we did the group of motions, and that was the combination of the orthogonal group—now that acts on R^n, preserves the linear structure, and preserves the inner product, so in particular preserves the origin of the vector space;

75
00:21:14,890 --> 00:21:45,298
而刚体运动群可以将任意点移到任意其他点，我们记作 M（或 G），它由全体平移变换与正交群 O_n(R) 组合而成，变换形式为 g(v) = Av + b，其中 A ∈ O_n(R)，b ∈ R^n。
and the group of motions is something that can take any point to any other point, which we called M (or G), and that consisted of all the translations together with O_n, so things of the form g(v) = Av + b, where A is in O_n and b is in R^n.

76
00:21:45,298 --> 00:21:52,697
我们看到平移群构成正规子群，其商群同构于正交群。
And we saw the translations formed a normal subgroup, and the quotient group was the orthogonal group.

77
00:21:52,697 --> 00:22:15,205
我们在很多情形下分析了刚体运动群，研究了它在集合上的作用：它作用在空间 R^n 上，或作用在 R^n 的全体直线上，可以作用在我们能想到的许多不同集合上；我们还分类了它的有限子群与离散子群。
And we analyzed the group of motions in a lot of cases, and looked at it acting on sets: it acts on the set R^n, or on the set of lines in R^n; it acts on a lot of different sets that we can imagine.

78
00:22:15,205 --> 00:22:28,850
这些内容都属于具体群实例的范畴。
And we also identified finite subgroups of it and discrete subgroups of it. So this was all in the area of examples like this, specific examples of groups.

79
00:22:28,850 --> 00:22:51,429
我们识别了——让我擦一下黑板——我们主要限制在与二维欧氏几何相关的二维情形：我们研究了 O_2 的有限子群，证明它们要么是循环群，要么是二面体群；接着我们研究了刚体运动群的离散子群，
So we identified—let me erase a little here—we restricted a lot because it was related to Euclidean geometry in dimension two: we studied finite subgroups of O_2, and showed they were either cyclic groups or dihedral groups.

80
00:22:51,429 --> 00:23:22,007
它们的形式为：其平移部分给出 R^2 中的离散子群 L，L 要么是 {0}，要么由单个向量的整数倍组成，要么由两个线性无关向量的整数线性组合生成——后者称为格点（lattice）。
And then we did discrete subgroups of the motion group, and they had the form that you got a discrete subgroup L in R^2, which was either {0}, or multiples of one vector, or integer combinations of two independent vectors—this was called a lattice.

81
00:23:22,007 --> 00:23:35,597
我们证明了平移群的离散子群只有这几种可能；接着在 O_2 中得到一个有限群——至少是一个有限商群（点群），它们同样被判定为循环群或二面体群。
We proved that those were the only possibilities for a discrete subgroup of the translations; and then you got a little finite group in O_2—well, at least a finite quotient group—and those we identified as either cyclic or dihedral.

82
00:23:35,597 --> 00:23:54,949
我们没有穷尽列出所有可能，但看到只有特定几何形态的格点，才能允许点群阶数大于 2；这就是离散刚体运动群。
We didn't classify all possibilities, but we saw that only certain lattices allow a larger group here than a group of order 2; so that was the discrete group of motions.

83
00:23:54,949 --> 00:24:06,043
[学生提问] 不，一点也不，这很重要！
[Student asks question] No, not at all, no, it's important!

84
00:24:06,043 --> 00:24:36,093
我们讨论了 O_2 的有限子群————这里严格来说不是记作 Γ，有一个群是运动群的离散子群……让我更精确地表述：如果这里有一个离散子群，记作 Γ_disc，那么 L 就是Γ 与平移群的交集：
So we discussed the finite subgroups— —and it's not really Gamma here, namely there's a group here which is the discrete subgroup... let me say it more precisely: if we have a discrete subgroup here, let's call it Gamma_disc, then this L is the intersection of Gamma with the translations,

85
00:24:36,093 --> 00:25:02,736
它要么是 {0}（不含非平凡平移），要么由单个向量的全部整数倍平移构成，要么由两个线性无关向量生成（格点）。我们发现，商群 Γ-bar = Γ/L 是O_2 中的有限子群（因为 M/R^2 ≅ O_2）。
which is either {0} (it has no translations in it), or translations by integer multiples of 1 vector, or translations by two independent vectors (a lattice). And we discovered that if we took Gamma-bar = Gamma/L, that was a finite subgroup in O_2 (since M/R^2 \cong O_2).

86
00:25:02,736 --> 00:25:20,843
这就是运动群离散子群的结构构成：首先得到一个平移离散子群，将其作为正规子群做商群，它是有限指数的，商群是 O_2 的有限子群，而这早已被我们分类完毕。
So that was the structure of a discrete subgroup of the motion group: first you got a discrete subgroup of translations, and then if you modded it out—if you took that as a normal subgroup—it was of finite index, and the quotient group was a finite subgroup of O_2, which we had already classified.

87
00:25:20,843 --> 00:25:40,228
这里的限制非常严苛，我们证明过你不能得到任意群：例如在 L 为二维格点的情形下，该子群的阶数至多为 12（晶体学限制）；它不能是任意阶的循环群或二面体群，
And this was very restricted; that's what we showed: you couldn't get an arbitrary group. For example, in the case where L was a lattice, the order of this subgroup was at most 12, we showed; so it couldn't be an arbitrary cyclic or dihedral group,

88
00:25:40,228 --> 00:26:01,069
因为它必须保持 R^2 中的格点 L 不变——当它作为O_2 中的元素作用在平面上时，必须稳定该格点。这给允许出现的循环群和二面体群施加了极其严格的限制。好，这只是梳理提点一下。
because it has to preserve the lattice L in R^2, namely when it operates on the plane as an element in O_2, it has to stabilize the lattice. And that put a very serious restriction on which cyclic and dihedral groups we could have, okay? So this is just a review to highlight it.

89
00:26:01,069 --> 00:26:15,320
期末考试中我不会要求大家证明这些结论，但我可能会要求回忆有限子群的结构，或离散子群的结构——要现场完整分类全部离散子群就太难了。
Now, I'm not going to ask you to prove any of this on the exam, but I may ask you to recall the structure of finite subgroups here, or the structure of discrete subgroups here—it may be much too difficult to classify all discrete subgroups, okay?

90
00:26:16,469 --> 00:26:47,802
好的，很好。接着我们研究了轨道计数公式在各类群作用中的应用，其中最重要的群作用就是群在自身上的共轭作用：G 通过共轭作用在 G 上，对 g ∈ G，定义 g(s) = g s g^{-1}。
Good. Okay, then we studied the applications of this formula to various group actions, and the most important group action is the group action on itself: G acts on G by conjugation.

91
00:26:47,802 --> 00:26:58,330
这是群通过共轭在自身集合上的作用，满足作用公理。
So if you have an element g, g(s) = g s g^{-1}. That's an action of a group on its own underlying set by conjugation that satisfies these axioms.

92
00:26:58,330 --> 00:27:19,695
元素 s 的轨道被称为 s 的共轭类（conjugacy class），它由所有形如 g s g^{-1}（g ∈ G）的元素组成；而 s 的稳定化子被称为 s 的中心化子（centralizer）C(s)。
And the orbit of an element s is called the conjugacy class of s, which consists of all elements of the form g s g^{-1} for g in G; and the stabilizer of s is called the centralizer C(s).

93
00:27:19,695 --> 00:27:26,820
由于这个群作用本身极为重要，它的轨道和稳定化子都有专门的专属名称。
So because this group action itself is so important, its orbits and stabilizers have their own names.

94
00:27:26,820 --> 00:27:50,719
随后我们利用这一作用分类了某些群，例如我们证明了 p^2 阶群必为交换群；对于 p^n 阶群，若 |G| = p^n，则 G 必具有非平凡中心 Z(G)。
And then we used this action to classify certain groups; for example, we proved that a group of order p^2 was abelian, and that a group of order p^n—if |G| = p^n, —then G has a non-trivial center Z(G).

95
00:27:53,309 --> 00:28:07,117
证明方法是将 |G| 写为各轨道大小之和（类方程），即 p^n 等于各元素 s 轨道大小之和。
And the way we did that was, we wrote |G| as the sum of the sizes of the orbits, so p^n is the sum of the sizes of the orbits of s.

96
00:28:07,117 --> 00:28:21,724
中心中的元素正是那些中心化子等于全群、轨道仅含 1 个元素的点；因此类方程化为中心元素个数 |Z(G)|（单元素轨道），
Now, the elements in the center are the ones where the centralizer is the full group, so the orbit has one element; so this becomes the number of elements in the center (where |O_s| = 1),

97
00:28:21,724 --> 00:28:40,568
加上非平凡轨道的指数 [G : G_s] 之和，即在此求和项中稳定化子的指数：要么稳定化子是全群使得指数为 1，要么指数不为 1。
plus the sum over [G : G_s] where this is non-trivial, namely in this sum where you have the index of the stabilizer: either the stabilizer is the full group and this index is 1, or it's not 1.

98
00:28:40,568 --> 00:28:48,597
现在，如果指数不为 1，且群阶为 p^n，则该指数必形如 p^k（k ≥ 1）。
Now, if it's not 1, and the group has order p^n, this number must be of the form p^k for k ≥ 1.

99
00:28:48,597 --> 00:28:56,295
特别地，左边群阶可被 p 整除，右边的求和项也可被 p 整除，因此中心阶数这一项 |Z(G)| 也必须能被p 整除。
In particular, this term (|G|) is divisible by p, this sum is divisible by p, and so this term (|Z(G)|) has to be divisible by p.

100
00:28:56,295 --> 00:29:04,119
而中心并非为空，因为单位元 e 始终在中心里（|Z(G)| ≥ 1）；因此中心里必包含更多元素。
And this term isn't 0 because you have at least one element in the center (the identity e); so you have to have more things in the center.

101
00:29:04,119 --> 00:29:15,797
这就是我们通过共轭作用，利用群在集合上的轨道计数论证的典型范例。
So that was a typical example of how we used this kind of counting argument for groups acting on sets, via this very important conjugacy action.

102
00:29:15,797 --> 00:29:23,056
这是一个非常值得重点复习的知识点。这是可能的。
That would be a good thing to review. It's possible.

103
00:29:23,056 --> 00:29:34,324
不要忽视……别光看……往年各届的考查侧重可能略有差异，但是————接着我们利用群作用的思想证明了西罗定理。
Now don't omit... don't look at... I mean, in previous years people do slightly different things, but— —and then we used the notion of group actions to prove the Sylow theorems.

104
00:29:34,324 --> 00:30:04,376
群论部分剩下的核心内容不多了：我们有西罗定理：若一个群的阶为 p 的幂次乘以与 p 互素的数（即 |G| = p^n · m，且 gcd(p, m) = 1），西罗定理指出：必存在 p^n 阶子群 H；
So we had really only a few more things in groups: we had the Sylow theorems, where you had a group whose order was a power of p times a number prime to p (gcd(p^n, m) = 1), and the theorem said: there exists a subgroup H of order p^n;

105
00:30:04,376 --> 00:30:27,920
所有此类西罗 p-子群彼此共轭；且西罗 p-子群的个数n_p 整除 m 且满足 n_p ≡ 1 (mod p)。这是至关重要的定理，大家应当看看证明思路——但不必死记硬背。
all such are conjugate; and the number of Sylow p-subgroups divides m and is congruent to 1 mod p. That's an important theorem, and you should look at the proof—I wouldn't memorize it.

106
00:30:27,920 --> 00:30:41,339
我们随后用它分类了 pq 阶群；考试中毫无疑问会用到这类论证。
And then we used that to classify groups of order pq; we will undoubtedly be using arguments like that on the exam.

107
00:30:41,339 --> 00:31:03,947
群论的最后一部分，我们深入探讨了对称群 S_n 中的共轭现象——S_n 是作用在集合 {1, 2, ..., n} 上的对称群，即 n 个对象的置换群。
And then we had the final section on groups, where we took a closer look at what conjugacy was in the symmetric group S_n, which is the symmetric group on {1, 2, ..., n}, permutations of n objects.

108
00:31:03,947 --> 00:31:23,922
我们证明了群中的任意置换元素都具有不相交轮换分解（cycle decomposition），各轮换的长度之和等于 n——
And we showed that any element in G had a cycle decomposition, where the lengths of the cycles summed up to n—

109
00:31:23,922 --> 00:31:41,549
例如各轮换长度分别为 a_1, a_2, a_3，a_1 + ... + a_k = n，对应 n 的一个整数分拆（partition）。
you know, if this had length a_1, and this cycle had length a_2, a_3... a_1 + ... + a_k = n, so it was a partition of n.

110
00:31:41,549 --> 00:31:52,741
而轮换分解的型完全决定了其共轭类：两个置换具有相同的轮换型当且仅当它们在 S_n 中共轭，并且我们给出了具体的共轭构造。
And that cycle decomposition determined the conjugacy class, so two elements with the same cycle decomposition were conjugate, and we showed how to conjugate one into the other.

111
00:31:52,741 --> 00:32:07,501
因此不同的共轭类在对称群中完全由轮换结构确定；一旦知道轮换分解，你就能轻易求出置换的阶数以及各种性质，对吧？
So the different conjugacy classes in the symmetric group are determined by the cycle decomposition; and you can work out the order of an element and all kinds of things if you know the cycle decomposition, right?

112
00:32:07,501 --> 00:32:21,163
例如在 7 个文字的对称群 S_7 中，如果有一个置换分解为 (1 2 3 4 5)(6 7)，我想知道它的阶是多少，你能立刻答出阶为 10；
For example, if I had an element in the symmetric group on 7 letters S_7 and it looked like this, and I wanted to know what the order of that element was, you'd tell me right away: it has order 10,

113
00:32:21,163 --> 00:32:37,353
因为前一个轮换需要 5 次幂才变成恒等映射，而后一个轮换需要平方，且不相交轮换彼此可交换。因此利用轮换分解，对称群中的计算变得非常清晰明了。
because I'd have to raise this element to the 5th power to be trivial, and this element I'd have to square it, and the elements commute with each other. So computations in the symmetric group become quite nice if one has this cycle decomposition.

114
00:32:37,353 --> 00:32:52,396
另外我还想补充一点：我们还研究了单群（simple groups）——即不含非平凡正规子群的群。
And I should say we did one other thing with groups, namely we identified various simple groups—those are ones with no non-trivial normal subgroups.

115
00:32:52,396 --> 00:33:05,996
我们花了很大功夫证明了 60 阶交错群 A_5 是单群；我们利用正二十面体（icosahedron）的对称性对其进行了深入剖析。
So we made a big effort to show that the group A_5, which is a subgroup of the symmetric group S_5, is simple of order 60; and we analyzed it using the icosahedron.

116
00:33:05,996 --> 00:33:19,808
接着彼得进一步向大家展示了——我想彼得证明了 A_n，即对称群中指数为 2 的正规子群交错群 A_n，在 n ≥ 5 时都是单群。
And then Peter went on to show you—I think Peter showed you that, did you show them that A_n, which is a normal subgroup of index 2 in the symmetric group, is simple for all n ≥ 5?

117
00:33:19,808 --> 00:33:37,535
这是一族极其优良的单群族；这是我们初步引入但未过深展开的另一个专题。彼得，关于群论还有什么我没提到、但值得在这里强调的吗？
So this is a great family of simple groups, and that's another subject which we just introduced but didn't go that far into. Peter, is there material on groups that I haven't covered that would be important to stress here?

118
00:33:37,535 --> 00:33:46,745
所以如我所说，如果让我来梳理复习思路——这正是备考这种期末考试最有价值的地方：不是为了学什么新知识，而是为了把所学知识系统化整理，
So as I say, if I focus, if I try to organize my study—and that's what's really useful about preparing for an exam like this: it's not that you're going to learn anything new, it's that you're going to be able to organize the material

119
00:33:46,745 --> 00:34:14,975
内化为你未来思考的工具。我认为群论有抽象群理论、群在集合上的具体实现与作用、向量空间，以及具体的群范例。
for your own thinking in the future. I would say there's the abstract theory of groups, there's the realization of groups acting on sets, vector spaces, and then there are the examples.

120
00:34:14,975 --> 00:34:25,871
这些内容相互交织、互相启发，例如抽象的西罗理论让我们能分类具体实例——比如15 阶群等等。
And these things all feed on each other, because abstract Sylow theory lets us classify examples—for example, groups of order 15, etc.

121
00:34:25,871 --> 00:34:29,579
它们之间有极其丰富的互动，我建议大家按这个框架来串联知识。
So there's a lot of interaction, but I would piece it together that way.

122
00:34:35,149 --> 00:34:46,521
不不不，绝非如此。不，那难以置信！
No, no, no, absolutely not. No, that's hard to believe!

123
00:34:46,521 --> 00:34:56,263
课上讲的内容可能有些在教材里没有，或者课上讲得更好，但大家如果课上给出了不同的推导，在考试中不需要去默写阿廷（Artin）教材上的论证。
There may be things that aren't... that were better done in class, but you wouldn't have to repeat the argument in Artin if we gave a different argument in class, if that's the question.

124
00:34:56,263 --> 00:35:13,846
好了，趁着黑板还在，我们来谈谈向量空间。这是我们在讲解刚体运动群之前插入的一个过渡章节；在讨论内积以及严格界定群 GL_n(R) 之前，我们必须重温向量空间理论。
All right, while I have this up, let's talk a little bit about vector spaces, because that was the interim chapter that we did before we could talk about the group of motions, before we could talk about inner products or really what this group GL_n(R) was: we had to review the theory of vector spaces.

125
00:35:13,846 --> 00:35:24,978
我想期末考试对这部分只会轻量考查，因为我们重点要考查环论，而且向量空间大家此前大多学过。
So that'll be tested lightly, I think, on the exam, because I want to get to some of the ring theory, and vector spaces I think many of you have seen before.

126
00:35:24,978 --> 00:35:56,692
我们最初从实向量空间讲起，即欧氏空间 R^n；随后我们进行了抽象化：抽象向量空间是一个集合 V，在加法下构成交换群，包含单位元（原点 0）、每个向量的加法逆元 -v；
So we started off with real vector spaces, by which we just meant R^n. And then we thought about them abstractly: abstract vector spaces were just a set V which was an abelian group under addition, with the identity element (the origin 0), inverse elements -v,

127
00:35:56,692 --> 00:36:20,399
并且它带有一项额外结构：即带有一个抽象域 F——后来我们知道域是一类特殊的交换环，带有乘法单位元 1 且每个非零元素都存在乘法逆元（对所有 a ≠ 0 均可逆）。
and it had one extra piece of structure: namely, there was an abstract field F, which we later found was a specific type of commutative ring—it's a commutative ring with 1 where every non-zero element has a multiplicative inverse (all a ≠ 0 have an inverse).

128
00:36:20,399 --> 00:36:39,796
我们学过很多域的例子，如实数域 R、有理数域 Q 以及包含 p 个元素的有限域 F_p。我们证明了当 p 为素数时，商环 Z/pZ 确实是一个域。
And we had many examples of fields, like the real numbers R, the rational numbers Q, and the field of p elements F_p. We showed that, where p is a prime, this ring Z/pZ is actually a field.

129
00:36:39,796 --> 00:37:13,898
在谈论抽象向量空间时，必须先指定一个标量域，才能给出向量空间的定义：它是一个加法群，具有单位元 0 与逆元 -v，并且具有由域中元素 a 进行的数乘运算，即 v ↦ av；它在各方面对加法满足分配律。
And when you talk about an abstract vector space, you have to have a field specified before you can give a vector space: so it's an additive group with identity element 0, and inverse elements -v, and then you have a scalar multiplication by elements a in F, namely sending v to av; and that distributes with respect to the addition in various ways.

130
00:37:13,898 --> 00:37:33,291
我们证明了 R^n 是一个典型向量空间：取实数的 n 元数组，按分量进行加法，数乘运算 a · (v_1, ..., v_n) 就是把每个分量乘以 a。
And then we showed that R^n was a vector space where you took n-tuples of real numbers, added them as n-tuples, and scalar multiplication by a on (v_1, ..., v_n) was just taking the multiple of each coordinate.

131
00:37:33,291 --> 00:37:49,233
更一般地，向量空间的另一个基本范例是域 F 上的 n 元数组空间 F^n，这是实向量空间的推广。
And more generally, another example of a vector space is just n-tuples of elements in your field F^n—that was the generalization of real vector spaces.

132
00:37:49,233 --> 00:38:11,137
接着我们建立了基（basis）、线性无关与生成集理论，证明了若 V 具有有限生成集——即能找到一组向量 v_1 到 v_n，
And then we developed the theory of bases, linear independence, and spanning sets, to show that if V has a finite spanning set over F—namely we can find a collection of vectors v_1 through

133
00:38:11,137 --> 00:38:35,760
使得任意 v 均可表示为线性组合 ∑ a_i v_i——若具有有限生成集，则 V 同构于某个 F^m，其中 m ≤ n，n 为生成集中的元素个数。
v_n such that any v has the form ∑ a_i v_i, a linear combination of those—if it has a finite spanning set, then V is isomorphic to F^m for some m ≤ n, where n is the number of elements in the spanning set.

134
00:38:35,760 --> 00:38:43,763
这个 m 是通过从生成集中剔除多余向量、直至剩余向量线性无关构成基来确定的。
And this m was determined by throwing out elements in the spanning set until they became linearly independent, forming a basis.

135
00:38:43,763 --> 00:39:00,650
因此我们有生成与线性无关这两个概念；我们证明了生成空间所需的向量个数必然大于或等于 m，而空间中线性无关向量的个数必然小于或等于 m。
So we have the two notions of spanning and linear independence, and we showed that the number of elements required to span the space was greater than or equal to m, and the number of elements which could be linearly independent in the space was less than or equal to m.

136
00:39:00,650 --> 00:39:11,558
如果一个集合既能生成空间又线性无关，就称为基；并且同一空间的所有基都包含相同数量的向量。
And if you had a set that both spanned and was linearly independent, that was called a basis; all bases had the same number of elements.

137
00:39:11,558 --> 00:39:21,000
若将元素 v 用一组基展开，其表达式是唯一的，其坐标对应 F^n 中的一个元组。
And if you wrote an element v in terms of a basis, that was a unique expression, and the coordinates of that element gave you an element in F^n.

138
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:33,942
所以这是一个非常值得复习的核心结论：这一构造基本涵盖了所有有限维向量空间。但为了证明这一点，必须先证明每个有限维向量空间都拥有一组基。
So this is a really important notion to review: that this construction gave us basically all finite-dimensional vector spaces. But to prove that, you have to prove that every finite-dimensional vector space has a basis.

139
00:39:33,942 --> 00:39:40,572
因此请复习生成集、线性无关与基的定义，牢记所有基具有相同的元素个数。
So review the definitions of span, linear independence, and basis; know that all bases have the same number of elements.

140
00:39:40,572 --> 00:39:52,470
我不会要求大家复习全部线性代数来证明这些，但大家至少要清楚生成集的元素个数不小于基的元素个数，并且能够判断线性无关集。
I won't ask you to review all of linear algebra to prove this, but you should know at least that a spanning set has at least as many elements as a basis, and you should be able to identify linearly independent sets.

141
00:39:52,470 --> 00:40:11,609
是的，确实如此。既然我们弄清了所有有限维向量空间的结构，自然接下来就要考虑：向量空间之间的同态与同构是什么？
Yeah, exactly. So that being the case, once we identified what all the finite-dimensional vector spaces were, then it was natural to consider: what were the homomorphisms and isomorphisms between vector spaces?

142
00:40:11,609 --> 00:40:31,747
我们定义了向量空间之间的同态——称为线性变换（linear transformation）：它必须是加法群的同态，且与数乘运算可交换。
So we defined a homomorphism between vector spaces—which was called a linear transformation—to be a homomorphism of additive groups that commutes with scalar multiplication.

143
00:40:31,747 --> 00:40:46,520
我们证明了线性变换 T 的核（ker T）是 V 的子空间，T 的像（im T）是 W 的子空间，其中子空间的定义类似于子群。
And we showed that the kernel of T was a subspace of V, and the image of T was a subspace of W, where a subspace is defined analogously to a subgroup.

144
00:40:46,520 --> 00:40:59,212
我们证明了若 V 是有限维的，则 V 的维数等于核的维数加上像的维数（秩-零度定理：dim V = dim ker T + dim im T）。
And we showed that if V is finite-dimensional, the dimension of V was the dimension of the kernel plus the dimension of the image.

145
00:40:59,212 --> 00:41:09,179
这类似于群论公式：群的阶等于正规子群阶乘上商群的阶。
And that was like our formula: |G| = |H| · [G:H], the order of the group is the order of the normal subgroup times the order of the quotient group.

146
00:41:09,179 --> 00:41:11,830
所以这是一个极为重要且随处使用的维数公式。
So that was an important dimension formula which is used all the time.

147
00:41:11,830 --> 00:41:35,857
顺便提一下，我们还特别考察了：一旦这些空间是有限维空间，如果我们为 V 选取一组基 {v_1, ..., v_n}，为 W 选取一组基 {w_1, ..., w_m}，
And then we made a special consideration: we showed, by the way, that once these were finite-dimensional spaces, if we chose a basis {v_1, ..., v_n} of V and a basis {w_1, ..., w_m} of W,

148
00:41:35,857 --> 00:42:02,620
那么我们可以用一个 m × n 矩阵来表示 T；其记忆口诀是：如果你想知道第 k 个列向量是什么————将 T 作用在 V 的基向量 v_k 上，得到 W 中的一个向量，
then we could represent T by an m × n matrix, where the mnemonic is that if you want to know what the k-th column vector is— —you apply T to v_k,

149
00:42:02,620 --> 00:42:31,336
然后将它按 W 的基 {w_1, ..., w_m} 展开，得到坐标 (a_{1k}, ..., a_{mk})^T，其中 T(v_k) = a_{1k} w_1 + ... +a_{mk} w_m。
the k-th vector of the basis of V, giving a vector in W, and then you write it out in terms of the basis {w_1, ..., w_m}, and you get (a_{1k}, ..., a_{mk})^T, where T(v_k) = a_{1k} w_1 + a_{2k} w_2 + ... + a_{mk} w_m.

150
00:42:31,336 --> 00:42:50,408
一旦有了矩阵，你必须掌握如何由矩阵反过来确定线性算子；这把有限维空间之间的线性算子空间 Hom(V, W) 在加法下等同于全体 m × n 矩阵。
And once you have the matrix, you need to know how it determines the linear operator back; and that identifies the linear transformations Hom(V, W), if both are finite-dimensional, with m × n matrices under addition.

151
00:42:50,408 --> 00:43:18,365
接着我们更深入地研究了向量空间到自身的映射（自同态）：因为映射可以相互复合，从而构成一个环——V 的自同态环 End(V)；
And then we made a more detailed study of maps from a vector space to itself, because then they can be composed, giving a ring: the endomorphism ring End(V), usually a non-commutative ring of n × n matrices,

152
00:43:18,365 --> 00:43:30,168
这通常是一个由 n × n 矩阵构成的非交换环，矩阵乘法对应映射复合。特别是其中的可逆矩阵对应自同构。
where matrix multiplication corresponds to composition. In particular, the invertible matrices give the isomorphisms.

153
00:43:30,168 --> 00:43:44,936
我们学过：矩阵可逆当且仅当其行列式非零。记住这一点很有用，尽管我们并不会在行列式计算上出刁难人的题目。
And we saw that a matrix was invertible if and only if its determinant was non-zero. That's a good thing to remember, although we're not going to ask trick questions about calculating determinants.

154
00:43:44,936 --> 00:44:00,133
这正是 T 为同构的情形，而 V 到自身的全体同构构成一个群，记作 GL(V)，推广了 GL_n。
That's when T is an isomorphism, and the isomorphisms from V to V form a group, which we call GL(V), generalizing GL_n.

155
00:44:00,133 --> 00:44:13,366
若 V 是域上的 n 维向量空间，这就是全体可逆n × n 矩阵群 GL_n(F)，即行列式在域中非零的矩阵。
And if V is an n-dimensional vector space over F, this is the group GL_n(F) of n × n matrices over the field which are invertible, namely their determinant is non-zero in F.

156
00:44:13,366 --> 00:44:24,683
我们对该群做过不少计算，并指出我们可以单独研究单个线性变换 T: V → V——并非整个群，而是单个变换——通过研究它的特征多项式（characteristic polynomial）：
And we made a number of computations with this group, and we showed that you could study a linear transformation from V to V one at a time—not the whole group itself, but just one transformation—

157
00:44:24,683 --> 00:44:56,486
即 det(xI - T)；若 V 的维数为 n，这是 n 次首一多项式：x^n -tr(T) x^{n-1} + ... + (-1)^n det(T)。我们证明了该多项式的根就是 T 的特征值（eigenvalues）。
by studying its characteristic polynomial: det(xI - T), which is a monic polynomial of degree n if V has dimension n: x^n - tr(T) x^{n-1} + ... + (-1)^n det(T). And we showed that the roots of this polynomial were the eigenvalues of T.

158
00:44:56,486 --> 00:45:10,080
这些内容对部分同学来说可能此前学过，但这是一次非常关键的复习：我们必须牢固掌握这类线性代数基础，才能进一步深入分析正交变换等内容。所以我希望大家掌握好这部分线性代数知识。
Now, all of this may have been a review for some of you, but it's an important review: we have to have that kind of linear algebra if we're going to go on and do detailed analysis of orthogonal transformations, etc. So I'll expect you to know this much of linear algebra.

159
00:45:10,080 --> 00:45:12,700
[学生提问] 请讲？
[Student question] Yeah?

160
00:45:17,260 --> 00:45:25,200
我从未真正分清‘计算’和‘证明’有什么截然区别；不过考试会更偏向抽象推导。
I've never completely understood the distinction between computations and proofs, but no, it'll be more abstract reasoning, I think.

161
00:45:25,200 --> 00:45:37,077
但我可能也会要求计算，比如求一个 2×2 矩阵的特征多项式之类，大家应该都要能算得出来。
But it's good—I mean, I might ask you to compute, but I wouldn't hesitate to ask you to compute the characteristic polynomial of a 2×2 matrix or something like that; you should be able to do that, okay?

162
00:45:37,077 --> 00:45:53,538
抱歉，有时有人会轻视纯代数数学家说‘噢，他只会做计算’，但如果不做计算，你又怎么能完成证明呢？
Sorry, sometimes people put down an abstract mathematician by saying, 'Oh, he just does computations,' but how can you do proofs without computation?

163
00:45:54,288 --> 00:46:01,330
在某种意义上证明也是广义的计算！彼得周五会更深入复习多项式理论及其根等等。
I mean, it's all computation somehow! So Peter will review a little bit more of the theory of polynomials and their roots, etc.

164
00:46:01,330 --> 00:46:13,423
但这与多项式理论无缝衔接：特征多项式是多项式环 F[x] 中的元素，它是研究线性变换的非常有用的不变量。
But this plugs into the theory of polynomials: this is a polynomial in the ring F[x], and it's a very useful invariant of the transformation that can be used to study it.

165
00:46:13,423 --> 00:46:25,761
它虽然不能完全决定相似类（共轭类），但我们确实指出过……我的意思是，我应当补充说明：如果你选用不同的基来表示 T，你会得到一个新的表示矩阵 T'，
It doesn't quite determine the conjugacy class, but we did show that... I mean, I should have said that if you chose a different basis to represent T,

166
00:46:25,761 --> 00:46:48,648
它具有形式P A P^{-1}，其中 P 是基变换的可逆过渡矩阵，实现从基 V 到基 V'的基变换（若是 V 到 W 则是 Q A P^{-1}）。
then you'd get a new matrix T' which has the form P A P^{-1}, where P was an invertible change of basis matrix from basis V to basis V' on V (and W to W' on W).

167
00:46:48,648 --> 00:47:02,190
特别地，若对 V 的某组基 T 的矩阵为 A，当变换基时，你会得到新矩阵——抱歉，刚才讲得有点乱，我们重新理一下：用矩阵 A 表示变换；若变换基，
And in particular, if you chose a matrix A for T with respect to a basis on V, and you changed basis, you'd get a new matrix—sorry, this is all wrong, let's try this again: we represent the transformation by a matrix A;

168
00:47:02,190 --> 00:47:22,159
我们得到矩阵 B A B^{-1}，这是一个不同的矩阵，但具有这种相似形状。特别地，在 V 上换基得到新矩阵 A'形如 B A B^{-1}。
if we change basis, we get a matrix B A B^{-1} (or P A P^{-1}), a different matrix, but it would have this shape. And in particular, if we change basis on V, we get a matrix A' that looks like B A B^{-1}.

169
00:47:22,159 --> 00:47:31,621
事实证明，特征多项式仅依赖于线性变换本身：新矩阵的特征多项式与原矩阵的特征多项式完全相同！
And it turns out that the characteristic polynomial depends only on the transformation: the characteristic polynomial of this matrix is the same as the characteristic polynomial of that matrix.

170
00:47:31,621 --> 00:47:54,609
你可以利用行列式的性质自行验证：因为det(BA) 与 det(AB) 相等：虽然矩阵乘法不可交换，但行列式是可交换的，因为两者都等于det(A) · det(B)，而一旦进入底域，元素相乘是满足交换律的。
And you can prove that to yourself by the fact that the determinant—the determinant of BA is the same as the determinant of AB: even though matrices don't commute, the determinant is commutative, because both are equal to det(A) · det(B), and once you get down into the base field, elements commute with each other.

171
00:47:54,609 --> 00:48:07,653
这看起来要记的内容很多，但我想只要你用群论的语言来打包向量空间理论：线性映射就像群同态，其性质同同态如出一辙。
So this seems like a lot to remember, but I think if you package the theory of vector spaces in the language of group theory: linear maps are like homomorphisms, these are the properties of homomorphisms.

172
00:48:07,653 --> 00:48:17,589
向量空间真正全新的特点在于：在群论中，我们没有通用的自然方法去表示每一个群——我们知道如何表示循环群等简单群，但群一旦复杂起来，
The one thing that's really new to vector spaces is that, unlike group theory where we don't have a natural way to represent every group—we know how to represent cyclic groups and things of that nature,

173
00:48:17,589 --> 00:48:30,919
我们无法搞清所有群的结构；而在向量空间中，我们对所有有限维空间了如指掌！正是向量空间的这种坐标表示，使我们能够彻底剖析其间的线性映射理论。
but once groups get more complicated, we don't know what they all are—in the case of vector spaces, we know what they all are! And this representation of vector spaces allows us to completely analyze the theory of maps between vector spaces.

174
00:48:30,919 --> 00:48:41,424
既然我们连所有群都无法完全分类，指望分类群之间的一切同态是不可能的；但对于向量空间，我们可以利用基对空间完全分类；
So since we don't even know what all groups are, it's hopeless to classify all homomorphisms between groups; but for vector spaces, we can classify the vector space using a basis. Then using the basis,

175
00:48:41,424 --> 00:48:51,869
利用基建立起线性变换的优美矩阵模型，进而可以更深入地考察该变换，并通过特征多项式研究其特征值。
we get a nice matrix model of the linear transformation, and then we can investigate the transformation a little bit more closely, and its eigenvalues using the characteristic polynomial.

176
00:48:56,610 --> 00:49:08,122
是的，特征多项式正是这个行列式——一个 n 次多项式，是域上一元多项式环 F[x] 的元素。
Yeah, the polynomial is this determinant—a polynomial of degree n, an element of the ring of polynomials in one variable over the field F[x].

